Article 10 (Strategic Planning Headquarters)
(1) The Strategic Planning Headquarters shall have one director, who shall be a general officer. <Amended on September 5, 2017>
(2) The director shall be responsible for:
1. Military affairs concerning the National Security Council;
2. Assessment of strategic environments and threats;
3. Formulation and development of military policies, military strategies, and armament strategies;
4. External military cooperation;
5. Determination of force development requirements and acquisition and management of weapon systems;
6. Development of future warfare concepts, force structures, and weapon system planning;
7. Research on development of test and evaluation systems;
8. Preliminary review of test and evaluation plans;
9. Preliminary review of test and evaluation results;
10. Coordination and control of test and evaluation;
11. Review and execution of test and evaluation budgets;
12. Classification of wartime test and evaluation projects;
13. Guidance and supervision of joint combat development and joint education of the Army, Navy, and Air Force. <Amended on November 4, 2014; February 16, 2015>
